@startuml UC7_Validate_Privacy_Consent
!theme plain
title C4 Level 4 — Code Diagram: UC7 Validate Privacy Consent


class Patient <<Actor>>

package "iHOMIS Portal (React/Next.js)" {
    class "SavePage (Consent Section)" as iHOMISConsent <<React Component>> {
        + consentSigned: boolean
        + handleSave()
    }
}

package "WAH Hospital (React/Next.js)" {
    class "SavePage (Consent Section)" as WAHConsent <<React Component>> {
        + consentSigned: boolean
        + handleSave()
    }
}

package "ADAPT iPaaS Middleware (Golang)" {
    class IngestHandler <<struct>> {
        + mongoRepo: MongoDBRepository
        + HandleIngest(w: ResponseWriter, r: Request)
    }

    class MongoDBRepository <<struct>> {
        + InsertQuarantinedTransaction(tx: Transaction, msg: String)
    }
}

Patient --> iHOMISConsent : Reads DPA notice and ticks 'I agree'
Patient --> WAHConsent : Reads DPA notice and ticks 'I agree'

iHOMISConsent --> IngestHandler : if consentSigned===true: HTTP POST /api/v1/ingest
WAHConsent --> IngestHandler : if consentSigned===true: HTTP POST /api/v1/ingest

IngestHandler --> MongoDBRepository : if !consent_signed: InsertQuarantinedTransaction()
IngestHandler ..> Patient : HTTP 422 (if !consent_signed)

note right of iHOMISConsent
  State: consentSigned (default false).
  Only proceeds to fetch('/api/ingest') 
  if consentSigned===true.
end note

note bottom of IngestHandler
  Server-side second layer of enforcement.
  Reads consent_signed from request body.
  Error message references RA 10173 explicitly.
end note

note top of IngestHandler
  This use case is an <<include>> of UC6: Translate Data.
  Consent is enforced at two layers:
  1. Frontend UI: blocks form submission if checkbox is not checked.
  2. Backend API: ADAPT iPaaS rejects and quarantines if consent_signed !== true.
  Legal basis: Republic Act 10173 — Data Privacy Act of 2012.
end note

@enduml
